WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
[MUSIC]

00:00:20.182 --> 00:00:23.294
If you looked at it in
1860 in the United States,

00:00:23.294 --> 00:00:27.985
the major occupations in the United States
were you were either a farm worker.

00:00:27.985 --> 00:00:31.296
And the second most important was
you worked as a maid, or a servant,

00:00:31.296 --> 00:00:33.500
or something in somebody's house.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.550
By 1900, in 40 years that
it changed dramatically and

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:41.500
people were in factories, working in
factories, they were industrial workers.

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:49.120
For rural areas have been depopulated, the
cities experienced a huge boom in growth,

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:51.120
and that caused all kinds of problems.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:55.988
There was a gilded age,
too much money, too many immigrants,

00:00:55.988 --> 00:00:59.994
anti immigrant stuff,
the Democratic party platform of 1896,

00:00:59.994 --> 00:01:03.640
says we got to prohibit
proper labor from coming in.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:06.040
So all of that's happening
in the same sort of way.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.530
Too much wealth, too much inequality.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:11.560
All the same sorts of issues were present.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:14.850
But by 1950,
if you looked out that world today,

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:18.690
across the industrial world Europe,
United States, etc.

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:25.590
Those people that were in industrial jobs,
had good jobs, they had reasonable wages,

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:30.710
they had unemployment compensation,
they had healthcare, they had pensions.

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:36.940
And then sort of beginning in the 1970s,
automation began to take those jobs away.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:40.150
Then of course, the supply chain
management, people began to look for

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:41.450
the lowest producer.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:47.920
Those jobs went away and
the equilibrium in the 1950s,

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.750
all across the world was sort of
left parties that were pro labor and

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:56.350
right parties bearing
degrees that were anti labor.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:02:00.370
And it could be multiple party systems,
like in Italy, or in France, or

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:05.090
it could be in Germany where
there's a left party CDU,

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:08.970
right party rather CDU,
a left party SDP, and

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:13.620
the FDP in the middle balancing them out,
turning politics one way or the other.

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:17.539
Or in the United States,
it's the Democrats, the left party and

00:02:17.539 --> 00:02:21.184
Republican but it was stable but
now that stability is gone.

00:02:21.184 --> 00:02:25.903
[MUSIC]

00:02:25.903 --> 00:02:30.853
